# Cloudflare Pages redirects. This file holds no rules on purpose.
#
# Do NOT add the usual single-page-application rule:
#
#     /* /index.html 200
#
# Cloudflare Pages does not need it, and the rule breaks this site.
# Two documented Pages behaviors are the reason:
#
# 1. "Redirects are always followed, regardless of whether or not an asset
#    matches the incoming request." A /* rule therefore returns index.html for
#    /assets/index-<hash>.js as well, so no script or stylesheet ever loads.
# 2. "Redirects are applied before headers", so a matching redirect discards
#    the rules in _headers, including the Content-Security-Policy.
#
# Pages already serves index.html for unknown paths, because this project has
# no top-level 404.html file. See "Single-page application (SPA) rendering" at
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/serving-pages/
#
# Add real redirects below, one per line, in the form:
#     [source] [destination] [code]
